1
00:00:03,208 --> 00:00:07,847
Open Interaction Center, Management, Numbers Not In Service.

2
00:00:07,847 --> 00:00:13,048
The list is empty until a call, a lookup or a person marks a number.

3
00:00:13,505 --> 00:00:16,766
Mark as not in service adds a number by hand.

4
00:00:16,766 --> 00:00:21,305
Enter it with its country code, and click Mark as not in service.

5
00:00:21,791 --> 00:00:24,370
The number is listed with what found it.

6
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:28,351
Here that is a person, and the list shows when it was last found.

7
00:00:28,351 --> 00:00:30,931
Two more numbers are added the same way.

8
00:00:31,497 --> 00:00:34,894
Search by number filters the list by digits.

9
00:00:34,894 --> 00:00:36,797
Press Enter to search.

10
00:00:37,247 --> 00:00:42,319
Allow dialing removes the mark, so campaigns can load and dial the number again.

11
00:00:42,319 --> 00:00:46,742
Use it when the number is back in service or belongs to somebody new.

12
00:00:46,742 --> 00:00:48,747
It does not call the number.

13
00:00:49,197 --> 00:00:54,957
To allow dialing for several numbers, select them, and pick Actions, Allow dialing.

